        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1483">

                <pb facs="1195" n="1079" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1079"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/257.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Nicaraguan Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Nicaragua</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-11-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 7, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that a contract providing for a loan of $1,500,000 to the Nicaraguan
                    Government by Messrs. Brown Brothers and Company and J. and W. Seligman and
                    Company of New York, was signed by myself and Messrs. Brown Brothers and Company
                    and J. and W. Seligman and Company of New York on September 1st. This contract
                    was subsequently submitted to the President of Nicaragua and the National
                    Constituent Assembly, and was duly approved by that body on October 9th. The
                    contract provides that this loan shall be secured by the customs receipts of
                    Nicaragua, which shall be collected by a Collector General of Customs nominated
                    by the bankers, approved by the Secretary of State, and appointed by the
                    Government of Nicaragua.</p>
                <p>As I am under telegraphic instructions from my Government to expedite this
                    matter, I have the honor to request that when the bankers shall have submitted
                    to your excellency for approval the name of the person proposed by them as
                    Collector General that you will take action thereon as early as may be
                    convenient.</p>
                <p>Respectfully I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Salvador Castrillo.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
